# Data Layer

Callers depend on repository interfaces, never on JSON files or a future Drizzle client.

- Define ports in `*.repository.ts`.
- Implement adapters in `json/` (and later `drizzle/`).
- Swap implementations only in `src/server/repositories/index.ts`.
- Parse at the boundary with Zod. Throw on invalid content. Do not silently fall back.
- Do not import `content/*.json` outside an adapter.

API handlers return this envelope:

```ts
{ success: true, data: payload, error: null }
{ success: false, data: null, error: "Human-readable message" }
```

```ts
// BAD
import projects from "../../../content/projects.json";

// GOOD
const projects = await getProjectRepository().findAll();
```
